{"id": "unknown-2026-11-15-012", "date": "2026-11-15", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "High altitude, bitter cold, zero drivers: autonomous trucks take on Tibetan mine", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/11/SANY_EACON_MAIN.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Finding qualified equipment operators is hard enough for most mining companies, and the extreme weather, punishing conditions, and oxygen-deprived air of the Tibetan mountains combine to make finding operators even tougher for the operators if this high-altitude copper mine – but SANY thinks they have a solution:", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/15/high-altitude-bitter-cold-zero-drivers-autonomous-trucks-take-on-tibetan-mine/", "type": "rss"}]}
